04:15:07.962 --> 04:15:08.962
Alright cutting myself off cause i've always
wanted to explain this thingy Mangaka’s

04:15:08.962 --> 04:15:09.962
do.

04:15:09.962 --> 04:15:10.962
Gege does it occasionally from what i've seen
and Yuki did it here.

04:15:10.962 --> 04:15:11.962
Its called “author's fiat" or "authorial
fiat."

04:15:11.962 --> 04:15:12.962
It refers to a situation in storytelling,
particularly in manga, where the author introduces

04:15:12.962 --> 04:15:13.962
a plot development or outcome simply because
they have stated it to be so, without providing

04:15:13.962 --> 04:15:14.962
a logical or organic explanation within the
narrative itself.

04:15:14.962 --> 04:15:15.962
Its often used to resolve complex or seemingly
unsolvable plot points, establish new rules

04:15:15.962 --> 04:15:16.962
or abilities, or make significant changes
to the story without a clear build-up or explanation.

04:15:16.962 --> 04:15:17.962
Some people think it can take away from the
story, but tbh I like it if its used correctly

04:15:17.962 --> 04:15:18.962
as it can truly add to the hype of what's
to come.

04:15:18.962 --> 04:15:19.962
I’d love to know your thoughts on it though,
so be sure to let me know down below!

04:15:19.962 --> 04:15:20.962
